{
    "spec_version": "v1.18",
    "identifier": "RP-AXE",
    "name": "RP-AXE: Ahistorical Xploration & Engineering",
    "abstract": "RP-1's realism stack with a lightweight, science-driven, exploration-first career replacing the RP-1 career plugin. Parts unlock free with science; engineering and exploration are the focus, not management.",
    "author": [
        "miskoltrans"
    ],
    "license": "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0",
    "$kref": "#/ckan/github/miskoltrans/RP-AXE",
    "$vref": "#/ckan/ksp-avc",
    "tags": [
        "config",
        "career",
        "total-conversion",
        "career-scaling",
        "physics"
    ],
    "comment": "depends = the complete RP-AXE environment, one name per installed module: (everything RP-1 Express installs MINUS RP-1) + the 21 curated expansion part mods + SCANsat, exactly the list RP-AXE-deps.ckan carries (regenerated from the live test instance's CKAN registry; tools/rebuild-instance.ps1 proves it installs headless). Transitive deps (Kopernicus, FAR, AJE, DynamicBatteryStorage, KerbalKonstructs, ...) are left to CKAN. GRAPHICS = RP-1 Express's HIGH preset (Parallax, Scatterer, RSSTextures16K, RSSVE-HR, DistantObject, PlanetShine, CanaveralPads) + PoodsMilkyWaySkybox: ~8 GB more than the Low preset. 'Scatterer-config-default' / 'Scatterer-sunflare-default' are used on purpose: the bare virtual names have many providers and a headless resolver silently drops them. SCANsat: the dev instance runs the miskoltrans/SCANsat-GPU fork (not on CKAN); the public dependency is stock CKAN SCANsat, which carries the same part names the tree places. Conflicts with RP-1: RP-AXE replaces RP-1's career plugin.",
